        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hafiz Rashid Khan\n- Places: Bangladesh, Chittagong Hill Tracts\n- Roles: poet, author, editor, journalist\n- Concepts: postcolonialism, postcolonial studies, anti-military voice, colonialism, neocolonialism\n\nFacts:\n- Hafiz Rashid Khan was born on June 23, 1961.\n- Hafiz Rashid Khan is a Bangladeshi postcolonialist poet, author, editor, and journalist.\n- Hafiz Rashid Khan is known for his postcolonialism and anti-military voice.\n- Hafiz Rashid Khan was reputed for working in the tribal area of the Chittagong Hill Tracts in Bangladesh.\n- Postcolonial studies draw from postmodern schools of thought.\n- Postcolonial studies analyze the politics of knowledge, including its creation, control, and distribution.\n- Postcolonial studies examine the social and political power relations that sustain colonialism and neocolonialism.\n- Postcolonial studies examine how imperial regimes depict the colonizer and the colonized in social, political, and cultural terms.",
